e longest the sequence may go without an element.","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"clock","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The clock that measures the gaps."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tolerance of the timer’s sleeps. Defaults to ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"name":"customError","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The error to throw when the timer fires. Defaults to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"TimeoutError.timedOut(duration:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","type":"heading","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the same elements that throws if the upstream goes quiet.","type":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The timer starts when iteration begins and restarts with every element, so it bounds the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wait for the first element and each gap after it, never the sequence as a whole. Elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pass through unchanged. When the timer fires, the upstream is cancelled and the sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws, without waiting for the upstream to respond to the cancellation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and elements it produces while the consumer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"busy are buffered, so the timer measures the upstream’s gaps. A duration of zero or less"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws before the first element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let clock = ContinuousClock()","for try await line in bytes.lines.timeout(.seconds(30), clock: clock) {","    handle(line)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TimeoutError"},{"text":" (or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"customError"},{"text":") when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration"},{"text":" passes between elements, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any error the upstream throws.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/Just/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)":{"title":"timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/just\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customerror:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Just\/timeout(_:clock:tolerance:customError:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"timeout"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"clock"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12_Concurrency5ClockP8DurationQa","text":"Duration"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"customError"},{"kind":"text","text":": (any "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","pr